    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "ADR\u2011002 superseded ADR\u2011001\u202f[ADR-001#0.0] [ADR-002#0.0].  \nRedis now runs with a replica and Sentinel setup\u202f[ADR-002#0.0].",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M10",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The team that owns **search\u2011api** is **TEAM\u2011DISCOVERY**, whose lead is **Imene Djebbar**. [TEAM-DISCOVERY#0.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M11",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "Yes \u2013 the events\u2011bus (SVC\u2011EVENTS) was the root cause of the 2025\u201106 incident that delayed SMS delivery for up to 9\u202fhours [PM-2025-06]. The post\u2011mortem lists the follow\u2011up runbook **RB\u2011EVENTS\u2011BACKLOG** to address the backlog that caused the outage [PM-2025-06]. The runbook is directly linked to the service: SVC\u2011EVENTS \u2190[RUNBOOK_FOR]\u2192 RB\u2011EVENTS\u2011BACKLOG [SVC\u2011EVENTS]\u2190[RUNBOOK_FOR]\u2192 RB\u2011EVENTS\u2011BACKLOG.",
    "answer_judge": 0.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M12",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The notifications\u2011worker service (SVC\u2011NOTIFY) is owned by **TEAM\u2011ORDERS**, which is covered by the **ONC\u2011ORDERS** on\u2011call rota.  \nThe primary on\u2011call engineer for that rota is **Sara\u202fMeziane** [SVC\u2011NOTIFY][ONC\u2011ORDERS].",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M13",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 0.6666666666666666,
    "full": 0.0,
    "mrr": 0.5,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The Platform team received two action items from the post\u2011mortems:\n\n1. **From PM\u20112025\u201106** \u2013 \u201cTEAM\u2011PLATFORM will add a dead\u2011letter queue to every queue on the events bus by\u202f2025\u201107\u201115.\u201d [PM-2025-06#3.0]  \n2. **From PM\u20112025\u201103** \u2013 \u201cTEAM\u2011PLATFORM will run Redis with a replica and Sentinel by\u202f2025\u201104\u201130.\u201d [PM-2025-03#3.0]",
    "answer_judge": 0.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M14",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 0.5,
    "full": 0.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The Numidia\u202fPay client\u2011certificate expiry caused a failure in the **payments\u2011gateway** service (SVC\u2011PAYMENTS) \u2013 all card payments were refused for 2\u202fh\u202f10\u202fm until the certificate was renewed. Cash\u2011on\u2011delivery orders continued to work normally. [PM-2025-08#1.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M15",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 0.5,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "Checkout depends on the external provider **SVC\u2011NUMIDIAPAY** for card payments [SVC-PAYMENTS#0.0][SVC-NUMIDIAPAY#0.0].  \nIts certificate alert, **NumidiaPayCertificateExpiry**, is configured to fire **30\u202fdays before the certificate expires** (the alert will be added by 2025\u201108\u201131) [PM-2025-08#3.0].",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M16",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The orders\u2011service currently uses a pool of **40** database connections. [SVC-ORDERS#2.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M17",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The secondary on\u2011call for the team that owns **payments\u2011gateway** is **Lina Cherif**\u3010ONC-PAY#0.0\u3011.",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M18",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The only architecture decision that applies to **orders\u2011service** is:\n\n- **ADR\u2011004** \u2013 \u201cPgBouncer in front of main\u2011db\u201d (orders\u2011service gets a fixed pool of 40 connections) [ADR-004#2.0].",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M19",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 0.3333333333333333,
    "full": 0.0,
    "mrr": 0.3333333333333333,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 0.0,
    "answer": "The cart\u2011loss incident was traced to the Redis cache.  \n* Runbook to follow up: **RB\u2011REDIS\u2011FAILOVER**\u202f[RB-REDIS-FAILOVER]  \n* The root\u2011cause runbook that was originally used: **RB\u2011REDIS\u2011RESTART**\u202f[RB-REDIS-RESTART]  \n\nThe Redis service is a dependency of the checkout API, which is owned by **TEAM\u2011PAY**\u202f[TEAM-PAY]. The specific owner of the Redis service itself is not listed in the provided context.",
    "answer_judge": 0.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M20",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 0.0,
    "answer": "The June\u202f2025 events\u2011bus incident impacted the **orders\u2011delivery** service (SVC\u2011DELIVERY) \u2013 this is the only service explicitly marked as impacted in the post\u2011mortem graph path\u202f[PM-2025-06\u00a0\u2192\u00a0SVC\u2011DELIVERY] [RB\u2011EVENTS\u2011BACKLOG\u00a0\u2190\u00a0PM\u20112025\u201106].  \n\nThe post\u2011mortem notes that SMS messages were delayed by up to 9\u202fhours, but it does not specify how many SMS messages piled up. No numeric count is present in the provided context.",
    "answer_judge": 0.0,
    "faithful": 0.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M21",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 0.5,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 1.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The database behind **catalog-service** is **SVC\u2011MAINDB**.  \nIts owner team is **TEAM\u2011PLATFORM**, whose on\u2011call rota is **ONC\u2011PLATFORM**.  \nThe escalation contact listed in that rota is **Sofiane Larbi**.  \n\n[SVC\u2011MAINDB#0.0] \u2192 [ONC\u2011PLATFORM#0.0]",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M22",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 0.0,
    "ctx_fact": 0.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The decision that changed how Redis runs is **ADR\u2011002 \u2013 \u201cDecision: Redis with a replica and Sentinel\u201d** [ADR-002#1.0].  \n\nThe runbook for Redis failover (RB\u2011REDIS\u2011FAILOVER) does not specify a target failover duration in the provided context.",
    "answer_judge": 0.5,
    "faithful": 1.0
   },
   {
    "id": "M23",
    "kind": "multi",
    "recall": 1.0,
    "full": 1.0,
    "mrr": 1.0,
    "fact": 1.0,
    "ctx_fact": 1.0,
    "answer_fact": 0.0,
    "grounded": 1.0,
    "answer": "The storefront\u2019s only dependency that is owned by the Checkout & Payments team is **SVC\u2011CHECKOUT** (checkout\u2011api)\u3010SVC-STOREFRONT#0.0\u3011\u3010SVC-CHECKOUT#0.0\u3011.",
    "answer_judge": 1.0,
    "faithful": 1.0
   }
